  "body": "## What is needed\n\nAfter `#1867` (`Pocket`, `Adaptive2D`, `Offset2D` on sketches) and `#1868` (`Slot` and `TrochoidalSlot` on sketches) merge, quick ops need the remaining common 2D mill shapes and operations.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Depends on the parametric sketch recipe slice (first sub-issue of `#3045`), `#1867`, and `#1868`.\n\n## Design\n\n- Extend `SketchRecipe` in `camcraft-geometry` with:\n  - Arc slot (centre XY, arc radius, start angle, angular span, slot width).\n  - Boss / outside frame (inner boss shape with corner radius and outer stock boundary).\n- Wire `Pocket`, `Adaptive2D`, `Circular`, `Slot`, and `TrochoidalSlot` into the quick-op batch command, Stock/Sketch UI form, and MCP tool (`add_quick_op`).\n- Keep existing entry laws (helix, ramp, plunge), finish allowance (`stock_to_leave`), and stock verification on the resulting normal `Operation` entities.\n- Refuse degenerate geometry (arc span zero or full self-overlap, cutter wider than slot or pocket) by name.\n\nClean-room rule: use plain machining terms only. Do not copy vendor UI labels, parameter names, or dialog flows.\n\n**Safety floor:** generates 2D clearing and slotting toolpaths and posted G-code (`effort:high`).\n\n**Done means:** a rectangular pocket, circular pocket, outside boss/frame, straight slot, and arc slot generate, verify against stock, post G-code, edit via `EditSketchRecipe`, undo in one step, and pass MCP tests with no 3D model.\n\nPart of #3045\n",
